Commentary of al-Nasafi (Madarik al-Tanzil) on surah 3, verse 16:

﴿Those who say﴾ is in the accusative case as a mode of praise, or in the nominative, or in the genitive as an attribute of "the God-fearing" or of "the servants."

﴿"Our Lord, indeed we have believed"﴾ in answer to Your call;

﴿"so forgive us our sins"﴾ in fulfilment of Your promise;

﴿"and protect us from the punishment of the Fire"﴾ by Your grace.
